      'daten_amp_datenschutz': 'Data &amp; privacy',
      'lucenta_läuft_vollständig_au': 'Everything below is stored on this device until you delete it &mdash; with Sign in with Apple, also encrypted in your iCloud.',
      'aktuell_ist_nichts_gespeiche': 'Nothing is stored at the moment apart from your appearance setting.',
      'ergebnis_wiederherstellen': 'Restore a result',
      'hast_du_deinen_stelligen_erg': 'Wrote down your 10-character result code from another device? Enter it here to restore it &mdash; that way a result can move to a new device without an account.',
      'wiederherstellen': 'Restore',
      'eigene_daten_zurücksetzen': 'Reset my data',
      'hilfe': 'Help',
      'aus__wissenschaftlich_validi': 'From 50 scientifically validated statements (IPIP Big Five model). Every answer feeds into one of five dimensions; the result shows where you sit on a scale from 0 to 100 relative to the statements themselves, not compared to a population group. Like any self-report measure this is an estimate with natural variation, not an exact fixed number — take the values as a reliable tendency, not as precise to the point.',
      'weil_die_berechnung_jede_ant': 'Because the calculation treats every answer equally, without judging how it came about. Some of the 50 statements are reverse-keyed (&ldquo;Don\'t talk a lot&rdquo; counts against &ldquo;Start conversations&rdquo;) — but that reversal is represented to different degrees in each dimension, exactly as in the original scientific questionnaire. So choosing the same value throughout does not land you neutrally in the middle; you still get a pronounced profile. Lucenta points this out on the result page when your answering pattern was very uniform. The result only becomes meaningful once you answer each statement individually — including when two of them feel contradictory.',
      'jederzeit_über_test_wiederho': 'Any time, via &ldquo;Retake test&rdquo; on the result page. On a repeat, the app additionally shows how your result has shifted since last time. For a meaningful comparison, several months apart is worth it — week to week the dimensions count as stable, and a test taken shortly after the last one measures daily form rather than real change.',
      'ja_sobald_ein_ergebnis_auf_d': 'Yes. As soon as there is a result on the device, Lucenta asks before every new run who is taking it. In a guest run your result, your history and your profile stay untouched: the guest result is saved nowhere and appears in no trend line. Whoever wants to keep it takes the code shown under the result and opens it on their own device. That same code is what you need for the compatibility comparison.',
      'nach_dem_test_bekommst_du_ei': 'After the test you get a short code. If a second person enters their own code, the app shows an overlay of both profiles and a short read on where you are alike or different.',
      'ausschließlich_auf_diesem_ge': 'On this device only &mdash; details are further up under &ldquo;Data &amp; privacy&rdquo;.',
      'für_erwachsene_die_sich_selb': 'For anyone 16 and over who wants to understand themselves better &mdash; as a prompt for reflection. Lucenta is not a clinical instrument.',
      'dein_testergebnis_misst_stab': 'Your test result measures stable characteristics (traits) &mdash; research says these do not change from day to day. The daily check-in measures your current state instead: energy and mood fluctuate perfectly normally from day to day, independently of your profile. Psychology keeps the two concepts clearly separate, so Lucenta does too &mdash; a bad day changes nothing about your test result.',
      'ja_nach_jedem_berechneten_ve': 'Yes. Everyone whose friend code you paste under &ldquo;Friends&rdquo; stays saved there &mdash; tap them to see your comparison. The free version compares you with two people, Lucenta+ with as many as you like.',
      'eine_kurze_auswahl_an_wissen': 'A short selection of scientific notes matching the two strongest dimensions from your own result. No new sub-categories, just widely replicated findings at the dimension level, summarised plainly.',
      'über_lucenta': 'About Lucenta',
