      'js_ed_titel_form': 'The shape of your profile',
      'js_ed_form_a': 'Between your highest and your lowest score lie ',
      'js_ed_form_b': ' points — ',
      'js_ed_form_c': ' at the top, ',
      'js_ed_form_d': ' at the bottom. Clearly outside the middle: ',
      'js_ed_form_e': ' of five dimensions. ',
      'js_ed_form_weit': 'With a span that wide it is not the height of any single dimension that carries your behaviour, but the distance between them. So read the combinations above first — that is where it says what your corners do to each other.',
      'js_ed_form_mittel': 'That is a middling span: single dimensions stand out without the others disappearing. Your combinations above say about as much here as the individual scores do.',
      'js_ed_form_eng': 'With a span this narrow no dimension towers over the others. That does not make you unremarkable, it makes you mobile: what you do is decided by the situation more often than by a fixed leaning &mdash; which is exactly why your daily state says more about you than it does about most people.',
      'js_ed_titel_kopplung': 'Whether energy and mood go together for you',
      'js_ed_kopplung_a': 'On ',
      'js_ed_kopplung_b': '&nbsp;% of your ',
      'js_ed_kopplung_c': ' recorded days, energy and mood sit on the same side of your own average. ',
      'js_ed_kopplung_eng': 'That is tightly coupled: for you the two arrive together or not at all. Knowing that, you can stop explaining a bad mood on a tired day.',
      'js_ed_kopplung_teils': 'That is a loose link &mdash; they usually move together, but not reliably enough to infer one from the other.',
      'js_ed_kopplung_lose': 'That is remarkably independent: you have tired good days and alert bad ones. Two things that go together for most people do not for you.',
      'js_ed_kopplung_d': ' Of the two, your ',
      'js_ed_kopplung_energie': 'energy',
      'js_ed_kopplung_stimmung': 'mood',
      'js_ed_kopplung_e': ' swings more (',
      'js_ed_kopplung_f': ' against ',
      'js_ed_kopplung_g': ' scale points of spread).',
      'js_ed_titel_testtage': 'What kind of days you tested on',
      'js_ed_testtage_a': 'For ',
      'js_ed_testtage_b': ' of your runs there is a daily state from the same or an adjacent day. Your energy on those days averaged ',
      'js_ed_testtage_c': ', against ',
      'js_ed_testtage_d': ' across all recorded days. ',
      'js_ed_testtage_neutral': 'The difference is small &mdash; so your results do not come noticeably from unusually good or unusually bad days.',
      'js_ed_testtage_hoch': 'So you tend to test on your better days. That is not a mistake, but it means your result describes you in form rather than you on average. A run on a tired day would be the most honest next one.',
      'js_ed_testtage_tief': 'So you tend to test on your weaker days. Your result is therefore more likely to sell you short than to flatter you. A run on a good day belongs in the picture.',
      'js_ed_titel_fest': 'What holds and what moves',
      'js_ed_fest_a': 'Across your ',
      'js_ed_fest_b': ' runs over ',
      'js_ed_fest_c': ' days, ',
      'js_ed_fest_d': ' has stayed quietest: ',
      'js_ed_fest_e': ' points between your highest and lowest score. The furthest travelled is ',
      'js_ed_fest_f': ' at ',
      'js_ed_fest_g': ' points. ',
      'js_ed_fest_ruhig': 'Both figures sit within the range in which the same person answers differently on two different days anyway. Your profile holds.',
      'js_ed_fest_bewegt': 'The second figure is above what measurement noise alone explains. Whether a real change sits behind it, or a particular stretch of life, only the next run will show.',
      'js_ed_titel_naehe': 'Where you are closest to others',
      'js_ed_naehe_a': 'The dimension on which you differ least from the people you compared with is ',
      'js_ed_naehe_b': ' &mdash; on average ',
